<%#
# Key: subagents/tools/wait/description
# Purpose: Wait-for-subagents Tool description.
# Used: Included in a Tool or Tool-input specification shown to the model as the wait-for-subagents Tool description.
# Locals:
# - None.
# Constraints:
# - Must render non-blank.
-%>
Wait for selected subagents, or all subagents when omitted, until they finish, this check-in window ends, or a new user message arrives. A still_working response is expected when work exceeds the window or a message arrived; read any new message, then call again to keep waiting. A timeout is not an error and does not cancel work. A settled successful turn is returned as response. During newer queued, running, persisting, failed, or cancelled work, the latest successful result may appear as previous_response only for context. Inspect each status and keep waiting while selected work is active.
